why: four dataflow entries still read as open and three of them are
  LANDED STAGES — 4, 5 and 6. An open entry for finished work is the
  same failure as a phantom spec box: it makes the list lie, and the
  list is what the next agent reads before taking anything.

what: tick them with what actually landed, and — the part that
  matters — with what did NOT. Stage 6's entry asks for keyed state in
  an okay-persist backend, and that half was REFUSED with an argument
  in 6b (a replacement worker replays rather than restores) rather
  than forgotten. The entry has to say so, or the next reader will
  take it as missing work.

  And dataflow-fan-exchange closes by its own condition: it said to
  consider it only after dataflow-complete-panes, because that lane
  might remove the merge instead of parallelising it. It did — 122 679
  accumulators reach the coordinator where 2.9 million did, three
  orders under the exchange's crossover — so there is nothing left for
  an exchange to buy.

predict: no code, and the risk is that ticking a box hides a half that
  is genuinely missing. Every tick says what was NOT done beside what
  was.
